From: Rainshower258 <188022223+Rainshower258@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:34:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(daemon): spin main run loop so NSWorkspace app list stays
 fresh

The accept loop blocked the main thread, so NSWorkspace never delivered the
main-run-loop notifications that refresh runningApplications. Apps launched
or relaunched after the first lookup were never found (get_app_state then
bound to a dead pid and returned a null screenshot). Serve connections on a
background thread and run the main run loop instead.
---
 native/Sources/CUADaemon/main.swift | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/native/Sources/CUADaemon/main.swift b/native/Sources/CUADaemon/main.swift
index 8d21c6a..cf197cb 100644
--- a/native/Sources/CUADaemon/main.swift
+++ b/native/Sources/CUADaemon/main.swift
@@ -219,4 +219,11 @@ func runAcceptLoop() {
     }
 }
 
-runAcceptLoop()
+// Serve connections off the main thread and keep the main run loop spinning:
+// NSWorkspace only refreshes `runningApplications` from main-run-loop
+// notifications, so blocking main in accept() freezes the app list and apps
+// launched (or relaunched) after the first lookup are never found.
+Thread.detachNewThread {
+    runAcceptLoop()
+}
+RunLoop.main.run()
